Replace the approved routes for a node

Usage: headscale nodes approve-routes [OPTIONS] --identifier <ID>

Options:
  -c, --config <CONFIG>            Path to config file [env: HEADSCALE_CONFIG=]
  -i, --identifier <ID>            Node ID. gRPC mode requires the numeric identifier
      --log-level <LOG_LEVEL>      Log level (trace, debug, info, warn, error) [env: HEADSCALE_LOG=] [default: info]
  -r, --routes <ROUTES>            Comma-separated route list. Empty list removes approvals
      --server <SERVER>            Legacy admin HTTP URL. Falls back to `$HEADSCALE_URL`. Trailing `/` is OK [env: HEADSCALE_URL=]
      --token <TOKEN>              Legacy admin HTTP bearer token. Falls back to `$HEADSCALE_ADMIN_TOKEN` [env: HEADSCALE_ADMIN_TOKEN=]
      --address <ADDRESS>          Upstream gRPC address. If unset, connect to the local Unix socket [env: HEADSCALE_CLI_ADDRESS=]
      --api-key <API_KEY>          Upstream gRPC API key for remote addresses [env: HEADSCALE_CLI_API_KEY=]
      --unix-socket <UNIX_SOCKET>  Local upstream gRPC Unix socket used when `--address` is unset [env: HEADSCALE_UNIX_SOCKET=]
      --insecure                   Disable TLS certificate verification for a remote gRPC address [env: HEADSCALE_CLI_INSECURE=]
      --json                       Emit raw JSON instead of the default table view
  -o, --output <OUTPUT>            Output format. Empty for human-readable, `json`, `json-line`, or `yaml` [possible values: json, json-line, yaml]
      --force                      Disable confirmation prompts
  -h, --help                       Print help
